diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index 512e095..420f9ba 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -8,6 +8,29 @@ All notable changes to ashlr-plugin. Format: [Keep a Changelog](https://keepacha
 
 ## [Unreleased]
 
+### Added
+
+- `.github/workflows/auto-tag.yml`: reconciles the `package.json` version on a green main commit. It discovers required checks from the branch ruleset and classic protection, waits (bounded, ~9.5 min) for every required GitHub Actions check on the exact commit to report success, then creates `v<version>` with the ashlr-release GitHub App token so the tag-triggered release runs. Skipped required checks never count as green (the skip-job pattern reports success by design). Triggers on `package.json` pushes to main, on `ci` `workflow_run` completion for push events, and on `workflow_dispatch` (`gh workflow run auto-tag.yml`). The main CI run now also runs the seconds-fast `fast` gate on pushes so auto-tag has a real check to verify.
+- `scripts/benchmark-schema.ts`: schema validator for both `benchmarks-v2.json` copies (`docs/` and `site/public/`). Core fields written by `run-benchmark.ts` are checked strictly; the `benchmark-refs.ts` cross-repo sections are validated when present, and every record carrying a `pattern` field must hold a non-empty string so a malformed grep sample can never publish. CLI prints one `<file>: <path>: <problem>` line per violation and exits 1.
+- `scripts/fast-check.sh`: typecheck plus only the tests mapped to files changed versus `origin/main`, for sub-2-minute pre-push verification. On a clean main it runs the typecheck only.
+- `scripts/bin-shebang.node-test.mjs`: asserts every `package.json` bin exists and starts with `#!/usr/bin/env node`.
+- `scripts/resolve-command.ts`: resolves executables through PATH before spawning, so a missing tool fails with a clear `Executable not found` instead of a raw spawn error. `affected-tests.ts` and `resolve-mr-conflicts.ts` now spawn `git` and package managers through it.
+- Docs site `/faq` page plus a homepage FAQ teaser section covering the agent index, account requirements, data flow, savings semantics and per-host surfaces. The hero now shows the measured per-call figures (reads about −75%, greps about −27%) instead of a fixed "60% fewer tokens" claim, and links the `/llms.txt` agent index and the GitHub repo.
+- Contributor reference notes in `docs/`: grep pattern inventory, list, purpose, selection and language map for the benchmark's fixed workload; methodology and result locations; Rust match-rate interpretation and caveats; orchestrate Team-quota notes and open questions; the parallelize example comparison and reference; and pipe grep data-flow, output and walkthrough pages.
+
+### Changed
+
+- Every default MCP tool's `description` was rewritten shorter, shrinking the `tools/list` payload an agent downloads on every session start. Tool names, input schemas and call results are unchanged; `servers/_tool-catalog.json` is regenerated by `bun run gen:tool-catalog`.
+- `.claude-plugin/plugin.json` now counts every `commands/*.md` file in its description: "39 slash commands" (was the 37 `ashlr-*`-prefixed commands; `/goal` and `/loop` ship in the plugin too). The marketplace metadata keeps the `ashlr-*`-prefixed count by convention.
+- `scripts/run-benchmark.ts`: `bootstrapCI` sorts a copy of the input so the seeded resample no longer depends on measurement order, and `aggregate` is exported for tests.
+- `release.yml` `workflow_dispatch` accepts a `version` input (`X.Y.Z`) in addition to `tag`; checkouts pin `actions/checkout` to a commit SHA and set `persist-credentials: false`.
+- `site/public/benchmarks-v2.json` now serves the same 2026-10-19 reference-run snapshot as `docs/benchmarks-v2.json`; it was still serving the April 25 run.
+
+### Fixed
+
+- `ashlr__search_replace_regex`: a pattern containing a real line break or an `\n` escape now enables ripgrep `--multiline` automatically during candidate discovery: `rg` rejects multiline patterns outright without it, so those searches silently found nothing. The replacement docs now also state that `$$` emits a literal `$`.
+- `ashlr__search_replace_regex`: ripgrep spawn errors, signal kills, timeouts after partial output and unexpected exit codes now surface as scan failures instead of reporting "no matches". Previously only exit code 2 counted as an error.
+
 ## [1.38.0] - 2026-11-02
 
 Accumulated release since 1.37.1: the `/ashlr-selftest` command, self-tuning compression, the companion handshake and doctor probes, lazy MCP tool loading, and reliability fixes for `brief-eval`, hook timing and macOS child-process waits.
